+# Phase 8 Plan 01: Service Login Role Rename and Pinned Migration Exemption Summary
+
+**The service login role is now `hestia_service` end to end, proven on a fresh Supabase database, and the append-only migration gate admits exactly the two in-place migration edits through blob-pinned entries that expire on their own.**
+
+## Performance
+
+- **Duration:** about 15 min (start time was not captured; estimated from commit timestamps)
+- **Completed:** 2026-10-26
+- **Tasks:** 2
+- **Files modified:** 32 (two of them renames), 4 commits
+
+## Accomplishments
+
+- `scripts/check-migrations-append-only.mjs` takes `--exemptions FILE` (default `scripts/migration-exemptions.json` inside `--repo`). An entry applies only while the merge base holds `fromBlob` and HEAD holds `toBlob`, removes only its own `M` or `D`+`A` changes, and prints an `exempt:` line. A missing file means no entries; invalid JSON, a non-array, bad keys, a bad path or a bad blob exit 2. With nothing exempt the output is byte-identical to before.
+- The DB class ran as written: two `git mv` renames and the four-token substitution over 26 files, plus the capitalised name in the schema comment. HEAD blobs equal the planned values (`356bd667...` role migration, `120a54f9...` schema), and the residual count fell from 1013 to 944.
+- A fresh `supabase start` applied the renamed migrations; `policies.integration.test.ts` and `api.integration.test.ts` passed (2 files, 69 tests); `pnpm db:types` left `apps/service/src/db/types.ts` unchanged; the stack was stopped with `supabase stop --no-backup`.
+- Ten new gate test cases (35 tests total in the file) and docs for the exemption (`docs/testing.md`, `docs/file-map.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`) and the local reset (`docs/development.md`).
+
